Package: lindos-setup
Version: 1.0.0
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0, lindos-core, xdg-utils
Recommends: lindos-compat, lindos-gaming, lindos-transfer, librsvg2-common
Suggests: lindos-settings, lindos-desktop
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos first-boot setup (Out-Of-Box Experience)
 A Windows-11-style first-run wizard for Lindos. At the new user's first login
 it lets them pick a Mode (Everyday, Gaming, Work, Creator, Lite), a default
 web browser (only browsers that are already installed are offered; Google
 Chrome is downloaded by the installer, or in the background later if the
 installer was offline), a dark or light theme, accent colour, wallpaper,
 taskbar alignment, an optional step to bring documents, bookmarks and more
 from a Windows drive or transfer folder (nothing is copied until the Transfer
 tool is opened), and privacy preferences, then saves everything through
 lindos-core with one batched privileged helper call.
 .
 The wizard installs nothing and downloads nothing: system updates, drivers,
 the browser, apps and Flatpaks are handled by the installer (its record is
 /var/lib/lindos/install-state.json), and it never runs in the live (USB)
 session or as the temporary oem account.
 .
 Run "lindos-setup --reconfigure" to go through the wizard again.
